id: pm-jev-t1h1
title: Detect calibration population and explicit-label drift without inference
description: "Compare current task/type/input-bucket distributions and later explicit labels against a frozen calibration cohort. Acceptance: unchanged cohort stays below predeclared thresholds; shifted fixture trips them; sparse labels report insufficient evidence; zero inference calls; exact model/question digest binding; bounded typed SDK and CLI with remedies; non-git public-copy validation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: calibration,drift,read-only
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:50:26.011Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T23:07:23.060Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:50:42.351Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against installed CLI 2026.10.25 and pinned SDK 2026.10.20, sibling README surfaces and pm-jev calibration/replay implementations. CLI owns tracker reads, authoring, formatting and status roles; no calibration-population sentry found. Calibration binds model/question identity; replay compares policies; pm-rl owns training and promotion. This feature only computes read-only cohort distribution/error diagnostics. No imports, exports, sync, journal, claims, checkpoint or shared-state mutations are introduced, so retry/CAS and native-state migration contracts are not on its path. Strict versioned input carries frozen thresholds and exact identity; no provider adapter. Planned checks: shifted/unchanged/sparse-label fixtures, digest mismatch, dense finite bounded schema fuzz, 500 seeded replay/serialization operation sequences, non-git CLI with no git in PATH, SDK-read public tracker copy with unchanged artifact hash. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-25T22:57:41.764Z",codex-agent,"Implemented strict frozen-cohort SDK and jev drift command. Focused checks pass (5 tests; 500 seeded sequences, 4000 steps); new source targeted coverage is 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Public-copy acceptance: 18 items, 42 verified authoritative files, task/type/input TV all 0 unchanged, controlled input TV 1 versus threshold 0.25, zero explicit labels therefore insufficient label evidence, zero inference/network calls. Second certified complete SDK read and artifact hashes unchanged. Public source and limitations are recorded in docs/calibration-drift-evidence.json. No native state is transformed; no import/export/sync or journal/concurrency path is added."
  "2026-10-25T22:58:35.823Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: temporarily disabled only population/error threshold crossings inside checkCalibrationDrift, leaving validation and output intact. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"predeclared sentries\" test/calibration-drift.test.ts failed with stable versus expected drift (exit 1). Restoring the implementation passes. Targeted adjacent run node --test test/calibration-drift.test.ts test/cost-policy.test.ts test/replay-command.test.ts passed 16/16 with no skips; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication passed. Schema boundaries include inclusive cutoffs and shipped example validation."
  "2026-10-25T22:59:22.492Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test runner executed the registered command successfully: 5 passed, 0 failed/skipped. Strict tracker health passes with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Ambient health reproduces existing pm-jev-v2la (pinned host 2026.10.20 versus global GitHub extension SDK 2026.10.25); no project extension, dependency pin or global installation was changed. Ordinary linked-file additions require repeated --add flags; links are now recorded. Implementation and local validation are complete; release verification is delegated to the unchanged CI npm/Bun matrix."
  "2026-10-25T23:00:02.516Z",codex-agent,Pre-review documentation pass corrected the Without git capability list punctuation. Full CI evidence will be linked in the PR; tracker item remains in progress and released for orchestrator verification.
  "2026-10-25T23:01:44.434Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary review added an own-index check for every array entry: a sparse SDK array with an inherited observation and an unrelated own property must be refused, even when its key count matches its length. Added an adversarial inherited-index regression; ordinary JSON behavior is unchanged. CI will rerun on the hardened head."
  "2026-10-25T23:02:19.559Z",codex-agent,"Hardened-head local checks pass: typecheck, test typecheck, lint and focused 5/5; targeted source coverage remains 100% in all four dimensions. Removing only the own-index condition makes the strict-boundary test fail (missing expected refusal, exit 1), proving the inherited sparse-array regression. Restored implementation; no inference or native tracker writes introduced."
  "2026-10-25T23:04:00.063Z",codex-agent,Bounded-file review now accumulates regular-file short reads until EOF or the fixed 8 MiB-plus-one buffer bound. This avoids accepting a valid JSON prefix if a regular-file read returns short before EOF; it also retains the concurrent-growth size guard. Rechecking the focused suite and numeric/schema coverage before the final CI head.
  "2026-10-25T23:05:42.368Z",codex-agent,"Final file-reader regression injects 17-byte read boundaries while retaining real regular-file bytes; it uses no SDK mocks. Reverting only the reader accumulation loop fails the host-handler regression (undefined status versus stable, exit 1); restoring it passes 5/5. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass; targeted source coverage remains 100% across statements, branches, functions and lines. Final CI head includes both own-index density and bounded EOF accumulation."
  "2026-10-25T23:07:21.733Z",codex-agent,"CI rejected the short-read commit at the committed-build check: its regenerated drift-command declaration source map was omitted. Included the generated map; no source behavior changed. Re-running the unchanged full CI matrix on the corrected commit. Earlier complete matrix on the own-index head passed, but is not counted as evidence for the final head."
